### [HIGH] Gallery.addFiles processes images sequentially with no parallelization  ·  `SAFE-AUTO` · effort M · conf 0.9
`src/components/Gallery.jsx L55-75`

**Problème :** Gallery.jsx L55-75 processes dropped image files one by one in a for loop with await on each file (await fileToWebp, await POST, setImages optimistically after each file). Uploading 20 images = 20 sequential encode-and-POST operations, which is slow (each file locks the next). The code also setImages([...images, ...added]) inside the loop iterations before the final saveJsonWithRetry, causing multiple state updates and re-renders during the process. Network/CPU are severely under-utilized.

**Correctif :** Use Promise.all or a bounded pool (4-6 parallel) to process files concurrently. Create a queue like `const results = await Promise.all(imgs.map(f => processImage(f)))` then accumulate results before the single saveJsonWithRetry call. Update status/progress once per batch (e.g., every 3 images) not per file. This divides upload time by ~4x for typical drag-drop batches.

### [HIGH] Marquee selection (rubber-band) fires recompute on every mousemove without throttling  ·  `SAFE-AUTO` · effort M · conf 0.85
`src/App.jsx L2029-2064`

**Problème :** App.jsx L2029-2064 defines the marquee selection handler. On every mousemove (L2062), it calls recompute() which calls setMarquee and setSelected (L2041). This happens at 60+ fps during a drag, causing React state updates on every frame. The recompute is not debounced or throttled; setSelected is called with a newly computed Set on every single mousemove. This causes massive re-renders of the IconTile grid during a marquee drag, even though most tiles haven't changed selection status.

**Correctif :** Throttle or debounce the recompute function: use requestAnimationFrame to limit recompute to once per frame (already partially done via rAF, but setMarquee/setSelected should batch). Or batch state updates: collect all selected IDs in a local array during drag and only update state once per rAF tick, not on every mousemove listener call.

